meta {
  name: 79 H2 INJECT pause the Debezium connector, and trigger nothing
  type: http
  seq: 79
  tags: [
    chaos
    local-only
  ]
}

put {
  url: {{connect_url}}/connectors/{{source_connector_name}}/pause
  body: none
  auth: none
}

script:pre-request {
  if (bru.getVar("chaos_watch_baseline_ok") !== true) {
    throw new Error("refusing to pause the connector: H1 did not prove the watcher alive and the connector probe ok first");
  }
  bru.setVar("chaos_watch_injected_ms", Date.now());
}

tests {
  test("Kafka Connect accepted the pause (HTTP 202)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(202);
  });
}

docs {
  ## What this proves
  DESTRUCTIVE: stops replication. The matching restore is `H7 RESTORE resume the Debezium connector`; send
  it even if a request in between fails. Unlike scenario A, nothing after this asks the pipeline to run: no
  DAG is triggered and no check is asked for the connector's state. Whatever raises the alert has to notice
  on its own.

  ## Captures
  - `chaos_watch_injected_ms` (pre-request)

  ## Consumes
  - `chaos_watch_baseline_ok` from `H1`
  - `source_connector_name`, `connect_url` (environment)

  ## When it fails
  404: the connector name is wrong. 409: a rebalance is in progress, send again.
}
